ic -->|Some terms missing| missing[**Incomplete**]\n            missing --> missingBC[**B = 0 and C = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 = 0 $$]\n            missing --> missingC[**C = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 + Bx = 0 $$]\n            missing --> missingB[**B = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 + C = 0 $$]\n            class missing fill\n      ","diagram-8G5ZSyxV0",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":310,"children":311,"id":315},{"name":242,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},[312],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":313,"data":314},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"Examples:","paragraph-XHQGtLEiX",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":317,"data":319,"storageKey":321,"id":322},{"name":318,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"blockMath",{"katex":320,"freeze":238},"\\underbrace{10x^2 = 0}_{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{x^2 + x = 0}_{C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{3x^2 - 8 = 0}_{B = 0}","$$ \\underbrace{10x^2 = 0}_{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{x^2 + x = 0}_{C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{3x^2 - 8 = 0}_{B = 0} $$","blockMath-CgF1K4LHA","incomplete-quadratic-equation",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":325,"children":326,"id":330},{"name":242,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},[327],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":328,"data":329},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"In that case, solving the equation is simple and fast. You can solve it manually or use general formulas:","paragraph-njyoRBEKh",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":332,"children":333,"id":337},{"name":303,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},[334],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":335,"data":336},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"\n      flowchart TD\n        bc0[**B = 0 and C = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 = 0 $$] --> bc0Roots[$$ x = 0 $$]\n        c0[**C = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 + Bx = 0 $$]\n        c0 --> c0Roots1[$$ x_1 = 0 $$]\n        c0 --> c0Roots2[$$ x_2 = -\\frac{B}{A} $$]\n        b0[**B = 0**\u003Cbr>$$ Ax^2 + C = 0 $$] --> b0Roots[$$ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{C}{A}} $$]\n        class bc0Roots,c0Roots1,c0Roots2,b0Roots fill\n    ","all-formulas",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":339,"data":340,"storageKey":342,"id":343},{"name":318,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},{"katex":341,"freeze":238},"\\overbrace{5x^2 = 0}^{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x = 0} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{x^2 + 3x = 0}^{C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_1 = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_2 = -\\frac{3}{1} = -3} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{2x^2 - 8 = 0}^{B = 0} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{-8}{2}} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ \\boxed{x_{1,2} = \\pm 2}","$$ \\overbrace{5x^2 = 0}^{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x = 0} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{x^2 + 3x = 0}^{C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_1 = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_2 = -\\frac{3}{1} = -3} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{2x^2 - 8 = 0}^{B = 0} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{-8}{2}} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ \\boxed{x_{1,2} = \\pm 2} $$","blockMath-D7mEhbM2D",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":345,"data":347,"children":349,"id":374},{"name":346,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"accent_important",{"title":348,"layout":264},"Do not memorize general formulas!",[350],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":351,"children":353},{"name":352,"type":237,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"accentMain_important",[354],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":355,"children":356,"id":373},{"name":242,"type":237,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},[357,360,370],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":358,"data":359},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"It may seem that since we derived general formulas, they must be memorized. This is not true. Do not learn them. Most people don't even remember them. The most important thing is -- ",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":361,"data":363,"children":365,"id":369},{"name":362,"type":247,"linkable":234,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"emphasis",{"type":364,"accent":234},"bold",[366],{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":367,"data":368},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234},"to be able to quickly notice that the equation is incomplete","emphasis-uoFty8bbQ",{"__TSPROSE_proseElement":234,"schema":371,"data":372},{"name":246,"type":247,"linkable":238,"__TSPROSE_schema":234}," (consists of one or two terms), which means it is solved quickly and simply!","paragraph-6sx7M8B3A","do-not-memorize-general-formulas",{"\u003Clink:global>\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it":376,"\u003Clink:global>\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it\u002Farticle\u002F$quadraticEquation":382,"$ B $":386,"$ C $":386,"$$ \\underbrace{10x^2 = 0}_{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{x^2 + x = 0}_{C = 0} >>{big} \\underbrace{3x^2 - 8 = 0}_{B = 0} $$":386,"$$ \\overbrace{5x^2 = 0}^{B = 0 \\ \\text{and} \\ C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x = 0} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{x^2 + 3x = 0}^{C = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_1 = 0} \\\\ \\boxed{x_2 = -\\frac{3}{1} = -3} >>{big}{top} \\overbrace{2x^2 - 8 = 0}^{B = 0} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{-\\frac{-8}{2}} \\\\ x_{1,2} = \\pm \\sqrt{4} \\\\ \\boxed{x_{1,2} = \\pm 2} $$":386},{"type":377,"content":378,"resolvedHref":191,"previewRequest":379},"contentItem",{"contentType":172,"contentTitle":190,"topicPart":231},{"type":380,"contentType":172,"topicPart":231,"fullId":381},"content-page","foundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fwhat-is-it",{"type":383,"schemaName":180,"elementTitle":195,"content":384,"resolvedHref":196,"previewRequest":385},"unique",{"contentType":172,"contentTitle":190,"topicPart":231},{"type":383,"contentFullId":381,"contentType":172,"topicPart":231,"uniqueName":194},null,[388,394,402,410],{"link":389,"schemaName":180,"title":263,"key":390,"seo":391,"description":393},"\u002Farticle\u002Ffoundations\u002Fequations\u002Fquadratic\u002Fincomplete\u00